## Accessibility Guidelines

### 1. Color Contrast (WCAG AA+)
- **Normal Text**: Minimum 4.5:1 ratio
- **Large Text (18px+)**: Minimum 3:1 ratio
- **Interactive Elements**: Minimum 3:1 ratio against background
- **Always provide text alternatives**: Never use color alone to convey information

### 2. Keyboard Navigation
- All interactive elements focusable via `Tab`
- Logical tab order (left-to-right, top-to-bottom)
- `Escape` closes modals and dropdowns
- `Enter` or `Space` activates buttons
- Arrow keys navigate within components (tabs, dropdowns)

### 3. Screen Readers
- Semantic HTML5 elements (`<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section>`, `<article>`)
- ARIA labels for icons and buttons without text
- ARIA live regions for dynamic content (new signals, P&L updates)
- Descriptive link text (no "click here")

### 4. Focus Management
- Visible focus indicators (blue ring, 2px)
- Focus trap in modals (prevent tabbing outside)
- Focus restoration when closing modals
- Skip to main content link (for keyboard users)

### 5. Reduced Motion
```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  * {
    animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
    animation-iteration-count: 1 !important;
    transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
  }
}
```

### 6. High Contrast Mode Support
- Test designs in Windows High Contrast Mode
- Use semantic color tokens (not hardcoded hex values)
- Ensure borders/outlines are visible

