## Design Workflow

### Phase 1: Discovery & Research (The Oracle, The Math)
1. Understand user needs and betting workflows
2. Review domain requirements (cricket betting specifics)
3. Analyze competitor products (Betfair, Bet365, Smarkets)
4. Define success metrics (conversion rate, time to bet, error rate)

### Phase 2: Information Architecture (The Architect)
1. Create site map and user flows
2. Define navigation hierarchy
3. Identify key user journeys (e.g., "Place bet from signal in < 10 seconds")

### Phase 3: Wireframing (Low-Fidelity)
1. Sketch layouts for key screens
2. Define component hierarchy and spacing
3. Review with stakeholders (The Oracle, The Architect)
4. Iterate based on feedback

### Phase 4: Visual Design (High-Fidelity)
1. Apply color palette and typography
2. Design all component states (hover, active, disabled, etc.)
3. Create dark theme mockups (primary)
4. Add realistic data and edge cases (long names, large numbers, etc.)

### Phase 5: Prototyping
1. Build interactive Figma/Framer prototype
2. Simulate key interactions (signal arrival, bet placement, P&L updates)
3. User testing with 3-5 target users
4. Collect feedback and iterate

### Phase 6: Handoff to The Architect (Developer)
1. Export assets (icons, images) optimized for web
2. Provide design specs (spacing, colors, typography)
3. Document interactions and animations
4. Pair with developer during implementation
5. Review builds and provide feedback (UI/UX QA)

### Phase 7: Post-Launch (The Guardian UI Tester)
1. Monitor analytics (heatmaps, session recordings)
2. Collect user feedback (surveys, support tickets)
3. Identify pain points and optimization opportunities
4. Plan design iterations

