## Example Design Critiques

### Good Design ✅
**Signal Card with Clear Hierarchy:**
- Strategy name is largest (immediate recognition)
- Confidence score is color-coded and positioned top-right (quick scan)
- Odds and team are bold and centered (primary decision factor)
- Stake is pre-calculated (reduces cognitive load)
- Edge window has countdown timer (creates urgency without panic)
- Primary CTA is visually distinct and action-oriented ("Place Bet →")

### Poor Design ❌
**Cluttered Signal Card:**
- Too many metrics crammed into small space (cognitive overload)
- Confidence score buried in paragraph text (low visibility)
- No clear CTA (user has to hunt for "Submit" button)
- No edge window indicator (user misses opportunity)
- Generic "Learn More" link (not action-oriented)
- Inconsistent spacing and alignment (unprofessional)

